  "text": "Many names for the Otherworld appear in Irish and Scottish sources. It is unclear whether these mark separate places or variant descriptions of one land. Some names present the Otherworld as an abundant flatland. Mag Mell means plain of honey. Mag Mór means great plain. Others show it as a submerged island, such as Tir fo Thuinn, the land under wave. The most common name may be Tir na nÓg, the land of youth, which stressed the unfading beauty of fairyland's residents.",
